---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../site';
---
<Base title={`About | ${SITE.name}`} description="Stayfile is a small set of free PDF, image and spreadsheet tools that run in your browser." path="/about/">
  <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>
  <p class="lede">{SITE.name} is a small set of tools for everyday file jobs, such as putting PDFs together or making a photo small enough to email.</p>
  <p>Most sites that do this ask you to upload your file first. That is an odd thing to ask when the file is a bank statement or a signed contract and your own computer could do the work. {SITE.name} does the work on your computer instead.</p>
  <p>It is built on open-source libraries: <a href="https://github.com/cantoo-scribe/pdf-lib">pdf-lib</a> for making PDFs, <a href="https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js">pdf.js</a> for reading them, <a href="https://github.com/jamsinclair/jSquash">jSquash</a> for WebP and AVIF images, <a href="https://www.papaparse.com/">Papa Parse</a> for CSV, <a href="https://sheetjs.com/">SheetJS</a> for Excel files, <a href="https://github.com/nodeca/js-yaml">js-yaml</a> for YAML and <a href="https://github.com/101arrowz/fflate">fflate</a> for zips. HEIC photos are decoded with libheif.</p>
  <h2>What is here</h2>
  <p>There are tools for PDFs (merge, split, rotate, number pages, turn pages into images and images into pages), for images (convert between JPG, PNG, WebP, AVIF, HEIC, GIF, SVG, BMP and ICO, compress and resize), and for spreadsheet and data files (CSV, TSV, Excel, JSON, YAML, Markdown tables and SQL). Each tool page explains the formats involved, and the <a href="/guides/">guides</a> go into the problems people most often hit with them, such as iPhone photos that will not open on Windows or a CSV that lands in one column.</p>
  <h2>How it is paid for</h2>
  <p>The site is free and shows ads through Google AdSense. The ads never see your files, because your files never leave your browser. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> for details.</p>
  <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
  <p>Bug reports and tool requests are welcome on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</Base>
